#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Start the ready tickets of a "new flow" convoy (T04, af-gfyj6k).

Spec af-wf4w5r §0 rule 3 and §4, user story 82: code, not the Mayor, starts
the ready tickets of a convoy that carries the new-flow mark, in dependency
order and under the ceiling N, through bin/dispatch-door, which records each
start. A convoy without the mark is not touched: the Mayor advances it as
before.

    convoy-advance CONVOY        one pass on that convoy
    convoy-advance --all         one pass on every open marked convoy, and on
                                 those closed outside acceptance or abandon
    convoy-advance --check-only  exit 0 if such a convoy exists, else 1
    --stopped-ok                 with CONVOY or --all: exit 0, not 3, for a
                                 stopped convoy whose incident is raised

One pass starts every ticket of the convoy that is open, not yet started
through the door, and whose blockers are all closed, while a place is free
under N. N (`max_sessions` in config/delivery-flow.json) is one setting for
the whole Factory, shared between the Specs. A place is taken by:

  - each live session of a delivery role agent (author, reviewer, Evaluator:
    config/delivery-roles.json), whatever the convoy;
  - each ticket of a marked convoy started through the door that no session
    has picked yet (still open): its author session is on its way.

A pass decides from the tracker alone, so a second pass on the same state
starts nothing more. Passes are serialised by a lock: two of them never
count the same free place.

A pass also merges (T18, af-gmz9s1; Spec §4): once the starts are made, it
hands each convoy that has a finished ticket to bin/spec-integration, which
merges one ticket into the integration branch of the Spec, runs the tests on
the merged result, and returns a ticket in conflict or red to its author. No
agent decides when a ticket is merged.

A pass also settles the reviews of criterion tests (T13, af-nkpjpr; Spec §5,
§8): it hands each convoy that has a review open, or a ticket that review
stopped and that did not reach the operator yet, to bin/test-review settle,
which launches once more a review left without result, stops the ticket
when the relaunch gave none either, and raises the stop through
bin/escalation-door. No author session has to be alive for that.

A pass also has the code of each finished ticket reviewed before its merge
(T14, af-96cusm; Spec §6, §8): it hands each convoy that has a finished
ticket not merged yet to bin/code-review settle, which sends the diff of the
ticket to a session of the reviewer role, sends it once more when the review
gave no result, stops the ticket when the relaunch gave none either, and
sends the answers given to its Blocking Findings to a second reviewer
session. bin/spec-integration merges nothing without a favorable verdict.

A pass also has each finished ticket evaluated on the launched product
before its merge (T15, af-higj9z; Spec §7, §8): it hands each convoy that
has a finished ticket not merged yet, or a launched product left to stop,
to bin/ticket-evaluation settle, which launches the product from a clean
copy of the ticket's commit, sends it to a session of the Evaluator role
(for a prefactoring: checks itself that the product starts), sends it once
more when the evaluation gave no result, stops the ticket when the relaunch
gave none either, parks a ticket whose criterion cannot be observed, and
stops the products once the states are in. Review and evaluation are sent
by the same pass: they run in parallel.

A pass also holds the single correction round of a ticket (T17, af-rx0ocp;
Spec §8): once the code review and the evaluation have both answered at the
tip and one refused, it hands the convoy to bin/correction-round settle,
which sends everything both refused to one fresh author session, and stops
the ticket still refused after that round, raised once to the operator.

A pass also closes the tickets (T19, af-iefuud; Spec §9): before the merge,
it hands each convoy that has a finished interface ticket whose fidelity was
not measured at its tip to bin/ticket-end fidelity, which runs the
mechanical fidelity check on the screens of its Validated Prototype; after
the merge, it hands each convoy that has a merged ticket still open to
bin/ticket-end settle, which closes the ticket once the nine conditions of
the ticket-end gate are met and leaves it open, with what is missing named,
otherwise. No agent closes a ticket of a marked convoy.

A pass also counts and bounds the resumes of a ticket (T20, af-y9pw9z; Spec
§5, §8): a ticket whose author session was interrupted (by its Ticket Exit,
or ended without one), that the merge returned, whose repair is closed or
whose request was answered is sent to one fresh author session on the same
branch, through bin/dispatch-door, and the resume is counted
(bin/convoy-state open-resume). At its third resume, whatever counted them
-- these, the correction round, a commit after a verdict -- the ticket is
parked with every ticket that waits for it and is not restarted; the others
keep starting. When nothing but parked tickets is left in a convoy, the pass
raises one request for the convoy, on a bead of its own, through
bin/escalation-door: it names each parked ticket and its cause. The answer
of the operator that lifts a parking is read by the pass, which lifts it
(bin/convoy-state lift-park): the ticket and those behind it are startable
again, with no hand on a ticket.

A convoy in an "état sans règle" (bin/convoy-state: a ticket started or
closed outside its door, evidence or a counter that cannot be read) is
stopped (T34, af-ckwina; Spec §0 rule 5): the pass starts none of its
tickets, writes none of them, and raises one factory incident, a bead of its
own that bin/escalation-door puts on the operator's list, naming the ticket
and the reason. The incident is recorded on the convoy through
bin/convoy-state, so the next passes on the same anomalies raise nothing
more. Once the state is valid again the pass withdraws the incident, closes
its bead and starts the ready tickets: no agent resumes the convoy.

A marked convoy does not close by itself (T22, af-kn83no; Spec §9): it is
closed only by code, on the operator's words. One found closed any other way
(bin/convoy-state list, `closed_outside`) is such an "état sans règle": the
pass walks it too, starts nothing in it and raises the same factory incident,
withdrawn once the convoy is open again.

Every answer is one JSON object on stdout. Exit status: 0 the pass is done
(what it started is listed, possibly nothing); 1 refused or could not run,
the dispatch door refused a ticket (named under `refused`), an incident
or a grouped request could not be raised or withdrawn, a resume could not
be sent, or the merge pass or the settlement of
the test reviews, of the code reviews, of the evaluations, of the
correction rounds, of the fidelity checks or of the ticket-end gate could
not run; 3 a
convoy is in an "état sans règle": nothing of it is started (0 with
--stopped-ok once its incident is raised: what the order runs, so that a
stopped convoy is not also an order failure);
4 the convoy does not carry the mark: nothing is started, nothing is written.
Settings, reads and the order that runs it: docs/CONVOY_ADVANCE.md.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import fcntl
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import tomllib
from contextlib import contextmanager
from pathlib import Path
from typing import Any, Iterator


PROGRAM = "convoy-advance"
BIN = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
ROOT = Path(os.environ.get("FACTORY_ROOT") or BIN.parent)
GC_BIN = os.environ.get("GC_BIN", "gc")
STATE_BIN = BIN / "convoy-state"
DOOR_BIN = BIN / "dispatch-door"
ESCALATION_BIN = BIN / "escalation-door"
INTEGRATION_BIN = BIN / "spec-integration"
TEST_REVIEW_BIN = BIN / "test-review"
CODE_REVIEW_BIN = BIN / "code-review"
EVALUATION_BIN = BIN / "ticket-evaluation"
CORRECTION_BIN = BIN / "correction-round"
TICKET_END_BIN = BIN / "ticket-end"
OPERATOR_CONFIG_BIN = BIN / "operator-config"
SETTINGS = ROOT / "config" / "delivery-flow.json"
ROLES = ROOT / "config" / "delivery-roles.json"
PROJECTS = ROOT / "config" / "projects"
DESCRIPTORS = ROOT / "config" / "project-descriptors"

EXIT_REFUSED = 1
EXIT_UNRULED = 3
EXIT_NOT_NEW_FLOW = 4
DOOR_DEFERRED = 75
# One ticket is merged per pass and per convoy: the merges stay serial, and a
# pass stays short however many tickets finished at once.
MERGES_PER_PASS = 1
# One interface ticket is measured against its Validated Prototype per pass
# and per convoy: a launch of the product and its captures take their time.
FIDELITY_CHECKS_PER_PASS = 1

# The stops the review of criterion tests writes (bin/convoy-state).
TEST_REVIEW_STOPS = ("test_review_refused", "test_review_no_result")

# The stop the code review of a ticket writes (bin/convoy-state).
CODE_REVIEW_STOP = "code_review_no_result"
# The stops the Ticket Evaluation of a ticket writes (bin/convoy-state).
EVALUATION_STOPS = ("evaluation_no_result", "evaluation_outage")
# The stop of a ticket still refused after its correction round (bin/correction-round).
CORRECTION_STOP = "still_refused"

# Spec §5: the exits that park their ticket; what the merge returns.
PARKING_EXITS = ("planning_exception", "operator_request")
RETURNED_MERGES = ("conflict", "red")
# Spec §8, K: a ticket out of resumes is parked for this cause (bin/convoy-state).
PARK_EXHAUSTED = "resumes_exhausted"
# The words of the operator for each cause of parking.
PARK_CAUSES = {PARK_EXHAUSTED: "reprises épuisées", "operator_request": "demande opérateur",
               "planning_exception": "Planning Exception"}

UNRULED = "état sans règle"
# bin/escalation-door refuses a field longer than this, or on several lines.
REQUEST_LINE_MAX = 140
CLOSING_GATES = ("ticket_end", "withdrawn")
RIG_RE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$")
# The publication door renders a ticket's rigs under this heading.
RIGS_SECTION_RE = re.compile(r"^## Target rigs[ \t]*\n+([^\n#]*)$", re.MULTILINE)


class Refusal(RuntimeError):
    """The pass cannot be made: nothing is started."""


class NotNewFlow(RuntimeError):
    """The convoy does not carry the new-flow mark; carries convoy-state's answer."""


class Deferred(RuntimeError):
    """The dispatch door deferred a launch: the next pass retries it."""


# --- reads -------------------------------------------------------------------


def run(argv: list[str]) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess[str]:
    try:
        return subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, cwd=ROOT)
    except OSError as exc:
        raise Refusal(f"impossible de lancer {argv[0]} : {exc}") from exc


def parsed(proc: subprocess.CompletedProcess[str], what: str) -> Any:
    try:
        return json.loads(proc.stdout)
    except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:
        detail = proc.stderr.strip() or proc.stdout.strip() or f"exit {proc.returncode}"
        raise Refusal(f"{what} a rendu une réponse illisible : {detail[-300:]}") from exc


def gc_json(*args: str) -> Any:
    proc = run([GC_BIN, "--city", str(ROOT), *args])
    if proc.returncode != 0:
        detail = proc.stderr.strip() or proc.stdout.strip() or f"exit {proc.returncode}"
        raise Refusal(f"gc {' '.join(args[:3])} a échoué : {detail[-300:]}")
    return parsed(proc, f"gc {' '.join(args[:3])}")


def read_bead(bead_id: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
    data = gc_json("bd", "show", bead_id, "--json")
    if isinstance(data, list):
        data = data[0] if data else None
    if not isinstance(data, dict):
        raise Refusal(f"bead introuvable : {bead_id}")
    return data


def marked_convoys() -> list[str]:
    """The open marked convoys, and those closed outside the acceptance and
    abandon commands (T22): a pass starts nothing in these, it raises them."""
    proc = run([str(STATE_BIN), "list"])
    answer = parsed(proc, "convoy-state list")
    listed = [answer.get("convoys"), answer.get("closed_outside")]
    if proc.returncode != 0 or not all(isinstance(ids, list) for ids in listed):
        raise Refusal(f"convoy-state list a échoué : {answer.get('error', proc.returncode)}")
    return [*listed[0], *listed[1]]


def ticket_rig(description: Any) -> str | None:
    """The single project a ticket targets, or None when it names none or several."""
    match = RIGS_SECTION_RE.search(description if isinstance(description, str) else "")
    rigs = [rig.strip() for rig in match.group(1).split(",") if rig.strip()] if match else []
    if len(rigs) != 1 or not RIG_RE.match(rigs[0]) or not (PROJECTS / f"{rigs[0]}.toml").is_file():
        return None
    return rigs[0]


def rig_repository(rig: str) -> Path:
    try:
        rig_dir = tomllib.loads((PROJECTS / f"{rig}.toml").read_text(encoding="utf-8")).get("rig_dir")
    except (OSError, tomllib.TOMLDecodeError) as exc:
        raise Refusal(f"config/projects/{rig}.toml illisible : {exc}") from exc
    if not isinstance(rig_dir, str) or not rig_dir:
        raise Refusal(f"config/projects/{rig}.toml ne déclare pas rig_dir")
    return ROOT / rig_dir


class Convoy:
    """A marked convoy as bin/convoy-state renders it, plus each ticket's rig."""

    def __init__(self, convoy_id: str) -> None:
        self.id = convoy_id
        self.load()

    def load(self) -> None:
        """Read the convoy again: a pass that parked, lifted or resumed
        decides the rest from what it wrote."""
        convoy_id = self.id
        tracked = [
            dep for dep in read_bead(convoy_id).get("dependencies") or []
            if isinstance(dep, dict) and dep.get("dependency_type") == "tracks"
        ]
        self.rigs = {dep.get("id"): ticket_rig(dep.get("description")) for dep in tracked}
        # Ticket branches live in the repository of the convoy's project;
        # convoy-state ties each verdict to its branch tip there.
        known = {rig for rig in self.rigs.values() if rig}
        self.rig: str | None = next(iter(known)) if len(known) == 1 else None
        repo = self.repo = rig_repository(self.rig) if self.rig else ROOT
        proc = run([str(STATE_BIN), "show", convoy_id, "--repo", str(repo)])
        answer = parsed(proc, f"convoy-state show {convoy_id}")
        if proc.returncode == EXIT_NOT_NEW_FLOW:
            raise NotNewFlow(json.dumps(answer))
        if proc.returncode not in (0, EXIT_UNRULED) or not isinstance(answer.get("tickets"), list):
            raise Refusal(f"convoy-state show {convoy_id} a échoué : {answer.get('error', proc.returncode)}")
        self.tickets: list[dict[str, Any]] = answer["tickets"]
        self.integration: dict[str, Any] | None = answer["convoy"].get("integration")
        incident = answer["convoy"].get("incident")
        # An unreadable record is one of the anomalies below, not a known incident.
        self.incident: dict[str, Any] | None = incident if isinstance(incident, dict) and "bead" in incident else None
        grouped = answer["convoy"].get("grouped_request")
        self.grouped: dict[str, Any] | None = grouped if isinstance(grouped, dict) and "bead" in grouped else None
        self.unruled: list[dict[str, Any]] = [
            *answer["convoy"].get("unruled", []),
            *({"ticket": ticket["id"], **anomaly} for ticket in self.tickets for anomaly in ticket.get("unruled", [])),
        ]

    def ticket(self, ticket_id: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
        for ticket in self.tickets:
            if ticket["id"] == ticket_id:
                return ticket
        raise Refusal(f"le ticket {ticket_id} n'appartient pas au convoi {self.id}")

    def awaiting_a_session(self) -> list[str]:
        """Tickets started through the door, or sent to a resume, that no
        session has picked yet."""
        return [t["id"] for t in self.tickets
                if (started(t) and t.get("status") == "open" and not t.get("exit")) or resume_on_its_way(t)]

    def not_started(self) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
        return [t for t in self.tickets if t.get("status") == "open" and not t.get("gates") and not t.get("exit")]

    def test_reviews_due(self) -> list[str]:
        """Tickets whose criterion tests are under review, or that the
        review stopped without the stop having reached the operator: what
        makes a settlement worth running."""
        due = []
        for t in self.tickets:
            review, stop = t.get("test_review") or {}, t.get("stop") or {}
            if (stop.get("reason") in TEST_REVIEW_STOPS and "raised" not in stop) or (review.get("request") and not stop):
                due.append(t["id"])
        return due

    def code_reviews_due(self) -> list[str]:
        """Tickets whose author has finished and that are not merged yet,
        or that their code review stopped without the stop having reached
        the operator: what makes a settlement of the code reviews worth
        running."""
        due = []
        for t in self.tickets:
            stop = t.get("stop") or {}
            if stop:
                if stop.get("reason") == CODE_REVIEW_STOP and "raised" not in stop:
                    due.append(t["id"])
            elif not t.get("park") and t["id"] in self.finished_unmerged():
                due.append(t["id"])
        return due

    def evaluations_due(self) -> list[str]:
        """Tickets whose author has finished and that are not merged yet,
        that still have a launched product to stop, or that their
        evaluation stopped without the stop having reached the operator:
        what makes a settlement of the evaluations worth running."""
        due = []
        for t in self.tickets:
            stop = t.get("stop") or {}
            if (t.get("evaluation") or {}).get("live"):
                due.append(t["id"])
            elif stop:
                if stop.get("reason") in EVALUATION_STOPS and "raised" not in stop:
                    due.append(t["id"])
            elif not t.get("park") and t["id"] in self.finished_unmerged():
                due.append(t["id"])
        return due

    def corrections_due(self) -> list[str]:
        """Tickets whose author has finished and that are not merged yet --
        their review or their evaluation may have refused them -- or that
        were stopped still refused without the stop having reached the
        operator: what makes a settlement of the correction rounds worth
        running."""
        due = []
        for t in self.tickets:
            stop = t.get("stop") or {}
            if stop:
                if stop.get("reason") == CORRECTION_STOP and "raised" not in stop:
                    due.append(t["id"])
            elif not t.get("park") and t["id"] in self.finished_unmerged():
                due.append(t["id"])
        return due

    def fidelity_due(self) -> list[str]:
        """Finished interface tickets, not merged yet, whose fidelity to the
        Validated Prototype was not measured at the tip of their branch:
        what makes a fidelity check worth running."""
        return [
            t["id"] for t in self.tickets
            if t["id"] in self.finished_unmerged() and t.get("interface") and not t.get("park") and t.get("tip")
            and (t.get("fidelity") or {}).get("commit") != t.get("tip")
        ]

    def merged_open(self) -> list[str]:
        """Tickets merged into the integration branch and not closed yet:
        what the ticket-end gate has to settle."""
        return [
            t["id"] for t in self.tickets
            if t.get("status") != "closed" and (t.get("merge") or {}).get("outcome") == "merged"
        ]

    def finished_unmerged(self) -> list[str]:
        """Tickets whose author has finished and that are not merged yet:
        what makes a merge pass worth running."""
        return [
            t["id"] for t in self.tickets
            if t.get("status") != "closed" and (t.get("exit") or {}).get("exit") == "finished"
            and (t.get("merge") or {}).get("outcome") != "merged"
        ]


def started(ticket: dict[str, Any]) -> bool:
    gates = ticket.get("gates") or {}
    return "dispatch" in gates and not any(gate in gates for gate in CLOSING_GATES)


def open_blockers(ticket_id: str) -> list[str]:
    return [
        dep.get("id") for dep in read_bead(ticket_id).get("dependencies") or []
        if isinstance(dep, dict) and dep.get("dependency_type") == "blocks" and dep.get("status") != "closed"
    ]


def live_sessions() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
    """The sessions that are not over, every convoy and Spec together."""
    answer = gc_json("session", "list", "--json")
    sessions = answer.get("sessions") if isinstance(answer, dict) else None
    if not isinstance(sessions, list):
        raise Refusal("gc session list n'a pas rendu de liste de sessions : le plafond ne peut pas être compté")
    return [entry for entry in sessions
            if isinstance(entry, dict) and not entry.get("closed") and entry.get("state") != "closed"]


def session_names(sessions: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> set[str]:
    """Every name a live session answers to (as bin/ticket-exit reads them)."""
    return {str(entry[key]) for entry in sessions for key in ("id", "name", "session_name", "alias") if entry.get(key)}


def role_sessions(sessions: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> dict[str, int]:
    """Live sessions per delivery role, every convoy and Spec together."""
    try:
        roles = json.loads(ROLES.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))["roles"]
        agents = {role: entry["agent"] for role, entry in roles.items()}
    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError, KeyError, TypeError, AttributeError) as exc:
        raise Refusal(f"config/delivery-roles.json illisible : {exc!r}") from exc
    counts = dict.fromkeys(agents, 0)
    for entry in sessions:
        template = str(entry.get("template", "")).rsplit("/", 1)[-1]
        for role, agent in agents.items():
            if template == agent:
                counts[role] += 1
    return counts


# --- settings ----------------------------------------------------------------


def load_settings() -> dict[str, Any]:
    try:
        data = json.loads(SETTINGS.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:
        raise Refusal(f"config/delivery-flow.json illisible : {exc}") from exc
    ceiling = data.get("max_sessions") if isinstance(data, dict) else None
    if isinstance(ceiling, bool) or not isinstance(ceiling, int) or ceiling < 1:
        raise Refusal(f"max_sessions (plafond N) absent ou invalide dans config/delivery-flow.json : {ceiling!r} "
                      "(attendu : un entier d'au moins 1)")
    start = data.get("start") if isinstance(data.get("start"), dict) else {}
    formula, role = start.get("formula"), start.get("role")
    if not isinstance(formula, str) or not formula:
        raise Refusal("aucune formule de démarrage (start.formula) dans config/delivery-flow.json : "
                      "aucun ticket d'un convoi marqué n'est démarré tant qu'elle n'est pas réglée")
    if role is not None and (not isinstance(role, str) or not role):
        raise Refusal(f"start.role invalide dans config/delivery-flow.json : {role!r}")
    # What the door receives to send a resumed ticket to a fresh author
    # session (T20). Absent: nothing is resumed, and a ticket to resume is
    # refused by the pass, by name.
    resume = data.get("resume")
    if resume is not None:
        if not isinstance(resume, dict) or not isinstance(resume.get("formula"), str) or not resume["formula"] \
                or not (resume.get("role") is None or (isinstance(resume["role"], str) and resume["role"])):
            raise Refusal(f"resume invalide dans config/delivery-flow.json : {resume!r} (attendu : formula, role)")
        resume = {"formula": resume["formula"], "role": resume.get("role")}
    return {"ceiling": ceiling, "formula": formula, "role": role, "resume": resume}


# --- the factory incident of a stopped convoy ---------------------------------


def passed(proc: subprocess.CompletedProcess[str], what: str) -> None:
    if proc.returncode != 0:
        detail = proc.stderr.strip() or proc.stdout.strip() or f"exit {proc.returncode}"
        raise Refusal(f"{what} a échoué : {detail[-300:]}")


def one_line(text: str, limit: int = REQUEST_LINE_MAX) -> str:
    text = " ".join(text.split())
    return text if len(text) <= limit else text[:limit - 1] + "…"


def anomalies_signature(anomalies: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> str:
    rows = sorted([str(a.get("ticket", "")), str(a.get("field", "")), str(a.get("reason", ""))] for a in anomalies)
    return "sha256:" + hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(rows, ensure_ascii=False).encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()


def operator_language() -> str:
    proc = run([str(OPERATOR_CONFIG_BIN), "language"])
    passed(proc, "operator-config language")
    return proc.stdout.strip()


def incident_request(convoy: Convoy) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """What the operator reads on the escalation door's list: the ticket and the reason."""
    first, others = convoy.unruled[0], len(convoy.unruled) - 1
    where = first.get("ticket") or f"convoi {convoy.id}"
    more = f" (+{others} autre{'s' if others > 1 else ''})" if others else ""
    return {
        "quoi": one_line(f"Incident d'usine : {where} — {first.get('reason', UNRULED)}", REQUEST_LINE_MAX - len(more)) + more,
        "pourquoi": one_line(f"Le convoi {convoy.id} ne démarre plus aucun ticket tant que cet état sans règle n'est pas réparé"),
        "que_faire": [
            {"option": "Faire réparer l'état par la maintenance de l'usine",
             "consequence": "Le convoi reprend seul dès que l'état est valide ; aucun ticket n'est avancé ni fermé à la main.",
             "recommande": True, "raison": "Le convoi reste arrêté tant que l'état n'est pas réparé."},
            {"option": "Laisser le convoi arrêté",
             "consequence": "Aucun ticket de ce convoi ne démarre ; l'incident reste dans cette liste."},
        ],
        "langue": operator_language(),
        "bloquant": True,
    }


def incident_description(convoy: Convoy) -> str:
    lines = [f"- {a.get('ticket') or 'convoi ' + convoy.id} : {a.get('reason', UNRULED)}" for a in convoy.unruled]
    return "\n".join([
        f"Le script d'avancement (bin/convoy-advance) a rencontré un {UNRULED} dans le convoi {convoy.id} : "
        "il ne démarre plus aucun ticket de ce convoi.",
        "", "Anomalies relevées :", *lines, "",
        f"Réparation : maintenance de l'usine, jusqu'à ce que l'état soit de nouveau valide (bin/convoy-state show {convoy.id}). "
        "Elle ne consiste jamais à avancer ou fermer à la main les tickets du convoi (Spec af-wf4w5r §0 règle 5).",
        "Dès que l'état est valide, bin/convoy-advance reprend seul le convoi, retire cet incident de la liste "
        "de la porte d'escalade et ferme ce bead.",
    ])


def record_incident(convoy: Convoy, bead_id: str, signature: str | None = None) -> None:
    argv = [str(STATE_BIN), "record-incident", convoy.id, "--bead", bead_id]
    passed(run(argv + (["--signature", signature] if signature else [])), "convoy-state record-incident")


def raise_incident(convoy: Convoy) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """One incident per set of anomalies, whatever the number of passes."""
    signature = anomalies_signature(convoy.unruled)
    if convoy.incident and convoy.incident.get("signature") == signature:
        return {"bead": convoy.incident["bead"], "raised": False}
    if convoy.incident:
        bead_id = convoy.incident["bead"]
    else:
        created = gc_json("bd", "create", f"Incident d'usine : convoi {convoy.id} arrêté ({UNRULED})",
                          "-p", "1", "-t", "task", "-d", incident_description(convoy), "--json")
        if isinstance(created, list):
            created = created[0] if created else None
        bead_id = created.get("id") if isinstance(created, dict) else None
        if not isinstance(bead_id, str) or not bead_id:
            raise Refusal("gc bd create n'a pas rendu l'identifiant du bead d'incident")
        # Recorded before the escalation: a pass that fails after this point
        # is retried on the same bead, never on a second one.
        record_incident(convoy, bead_id)
    request = json.dumps(incident_request(convoy), ensure_ascii=False)
    passed(run([str(ESCALATION_BIN), "benjamin", bead_id, request]), "escalation-door benjamin")
    record_incident(convoy, bead_id, signature)
    return {"bead": bead_id, "raised": True}


def withdraw_incident(convoy: Convoy) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """The state is valid again: the incident leaves the operator's list."""
    assert convoy.incident is not None
    bead_id = convoy.incident["bead"]
    passed(run([str(ESCALATION_BIN), "clear", bead_id]), "escalation-door clear")
    if read_bead(bead_id).get("status") != "closed":
        passed(run([GC_BIN, "--city", str(ROOT), "bd", "close", bead_id, "--reason",
                    f"État redevenu valide : bin/convoy-advance a repris le convoi {convoy.id}."]), "gc bd close")
    passed(run([str(STATE_BIN), "clear-incident", convoy.id]), "convoy-state clear-incident")
    return {"bead": bead_id, "withdrawn": True}


def settle_incident(convoy: Convoy) -> dict[str, Any] | None:
    if not convoy.unruled and not convoy.incident:
        return None
    try:
        return raise_incident(convoy) if convoy.unruled else withdraw_incident(convoy)
    except Refusal as exc:
        return {"error": f"refus : {exc}"}


# --- resumes counted and bounded, parked tickets, one grouped request (T20) -----


def state_write(*args: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
    proc = run([str(STATE_BIN), *args])
    answer = parsed(proc, f"convoy-state {args[0]}")
    if proc.returncode != 0 or not isinstance(answer, dict):
        error = answer.get("error", proc.returncode) if isinstance(answer, dict) else proc.returncode
        raise Refusal(f"convoy-state {args[0]} a échoué : {error}")
    return answer


def at_work(ticket: dict[str, Any]) -> bool:
    """Started through the door, not closed, neither parked nor stopped:
    what a resume or the bound of the resumes may bear on. A stopped ticket
    is never resumed: its sequence failed, it is with the operator."""
    return started(ticket) and ticket.get("status") != "closed" and not ticket.get("park") and not ticket.get("stop")


def resume_on_its_way(ticket: dict[str, Any]) -> bool:
    """A resume was sent and nobody took the ticket since: its session
    holds a place under the ceiling. A resume bead closed without the ticket
    taken is a session that ended: one more interruption, no place."""
    entries = (ticket.get("resume") or {}).get("entries") or []
    if not entries or not at_work(ticket) or ticket.get("status") == "open" or ticket.get("exit"):
        return False
    last = entries[-1]
    if not last.get("launches") or last.get("session") != (ticket.get("session") or {}).get("name"):
        return False
    return read_bead(last["launches"][-1]["bead"]).get("status") != "closed"


def resume_due(ticket: dict[str, Any], alive: set[str]) -> tuple[str, str, str] | None:
    """What the pass owes a ticket at work, read on the tracker alone:
    ("new", cause, ref) a fact that asks for a resume not counted yet;
    ("launch", cause, ref) a counted resume no session was sent for; None
    nothing, or a session on its way."""
    exit_record = ticket.get("exit") or {}
    exit_name, exit_at = exit_record.get("exit"), exit_record.get("at")
    session = (ticket.get("session") or {}).get("name")
    entries = (ticket.get("resume") or {}).get("entries") or []
    last = entries[-1] if entries else None
    if last and exit_name is None and last.get("session") == session:
        # Nobody took the ticket since its last resume was counted.
        if not last["launches"]:
            return "launch", last["cause"], last["ref"]
        sent = last["launches"][-1]["bead"]
        if read_bead(sent).get("status") == "closed":
            return "new", "interrupted", f"launch:{sent}"
        return None
    if exit_name == "interrupted":
        return "new", "interrupted", f"session:{session}" if session else f"exit:{exit_at}"
    if exit_name == "technically_blocked":
        return None if open_blockers(ticket["id"]) else ("new", "unblocked", f"exit:{exit_at}")
    if exit_name in PARKING_EXITS:
        # Its parking was lifted: the answer goes to a fresh session.
        return "new", "answered", f"exit:{exit_at}"
    if exit_name == "finished":
        merge = ticket.get("merge") or {}
        if merge.get("outcome") in RETURNED_MERGES and merge.get("ticket_commit") == ticket.get("tip"):
            return "new", "returned", f"merge:{merge.get('at')}/exit:{exit_at}"
        return None
    if exit_name is None and ticket.get("status") == "in_progress" and session and session not in alive:
        # Spec §5: a session that died without an exit is read as interrupted.
        return "new", "interrupted", f"session:{session}"
    return None


def launch_resume(convoy: Convoy, ticket_id: str, cause: str, rig: str, settings: dict[str, Any]) -> str:
    """Send the resume to one fresh author session: a bead of its own,
    routed through the dispatch door."""
    created = gc_json(
        "bd", "create", f"Reprise — {ticket_id}", "-p", "1", "-t", "task", "-d",
        f"Resume of ticket {ticket_id} by a fresh author session, on the same branch ({cause}).\n\n"
        f"convoy: {convoy.id}\nticket: {ticket_id}\ncause: {cause}\n", "--json")
    if isinstance(created, list):
        created = created[0] if created else None
    bead_id = created.get("id") if isinstance(created, dict) else None
    if not isinstance(bead_id, str) or not bead_id:
        raise Refusal("gc bd create n'a pas rendu l'identifiant du bead de la reprise")
    argv = [str(DOOR_BIN), bead_id, "--rig", rig, "--formula", settings["resume"]["formula"]]
    if settings["resume"]["role"]:
        argv += ["--role", settings["resume"]["role"]]
    routed = run(argv)
    if routed.returncode != 0:
        run([GC_BIN, "--city", str(ROOT), "bd", "close", bead_id, "--reason",
             "Reprise non routée par la porte de dispatch."])
        reason = (routed.stderr.strip() or routed.stdout.strip() or f"exit {routed.returncode}").splitlines()[-1]
        raise Deferred(reason) if routed.returncode == DOOR_DEFERRED else Refusal(reason)
    state_write("launch-resume", convoy.id, ticket_id, "--bead", bead_id)
    return bead_id


def park_exhausted(convoy: Convoy, ticket: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    resumes = (ticket.get("counters") or {}).get("resumes")
    answer = state_write("park", convoy.id, ticket["id"], "--cause", PARK_EXHAUSTED,
                         "--detail", f"{resumes} reprises, toutes causes confondues : le ticket ne redémarre plus")
    return {"id": ticket["id"], "cause": PARK_EXHAUSTED, "parked": answer["parked"]}


def settle_resumes(convoy: Convoy, settings: dict[str, Any], free: int, alive: set[str], out: dict[str, Any]) -> None:
    """Spec §8: park the ticket that took its last resume; send the ticket
    that needs its author again to one fresh session, and count it."""
    for ticket_id in [t["id"] for t in convoy.tickets if at_work(t)]:
        try:
            ticket = convoy.ticket(ticket_id)
            if ticket.get("resumes_left") == 0:
                out["parked"].append(park_exhausted(convoy, ticket))
                convoy.load()
                continue
            due = resume_due(ticket, alive)
            if due is None:
                continue
            what, cause, ref = due
            rig = convoy.rigs.get(ticket_id)
            if not settings["resume"]:
                raise Refusal("aucune formule de reprise (resume.formula) dans config/delivery-flow.json : "
                              f"le ticket attend une reprise ({cause}) que rien ne peut lancer")
            if not rig:
                raise Refusal("le ticket ne nomme pas un seul projet connu de config/projects sous « Target rigs »")
            if len(out["started"]) + len(out["resumed"]) >= free:
                out["waiting"].append({"id": ticket_id, "reason": f"reprise ({cause}) : plafond N={settings['ceiling']} atteint"})
                continue
            if what == "new":
                state_write("open-resume", convoy.id, ticket_id, "--cause", cause, "--ref", ref)
                convoy.load()
                ticket = convoy.ticket(ticket_id)
                if ticket.get("resumes_left") == 0:
                    # The third: parked with its descendants, not restarted.
                    out["parked"].append(park_exhausted(convoy, ticket))
                    convoy.load()
                    continue
            bead_id = launch_resume(convoy, ticket_id, cause, rig, settings)
            out["resumed"].append({"id": ticket_id, "cause": cause, "bead": bead_id})
            convoy.load()
        except Deferred as exc:
            out["deferred"].append({"id": ticket_id, "reason": str(exc)})
        except Refusal as exc:
            out["refused"].append({"id": ticket_id, "reason": str(exc)})


def request_answer(bead: dict[str, Any], since: str) -> str | None:
    """The letter the operator answered a request with
    (bin/escalation-door repondre), once it is no longer open."""
    metadata = bead.get("metadata") or {}
    option, at = metadata.get("gc.escalation_response_option"), metadata.get("gc.escalation_response_at")
    if metadata.get("gc.needs_benjamin") not in (None, "none") or not isinstance(option, str) or not isinstance(at, str):
        return None
    return option if at >= since else None


def settle_lifts(convoy: Convoy, out: dict[str, Any]) -> None:
    """An answer of the operator that lifts a parking is applied by the
    pass: any answer to the request an operator request left on its ticket;
    the option that accepts the deviation a Planning Exception asked about;
    the lifting option of the convoy's grouped request, for the tickets it
    names. Any other answer leaves the ticket parked."""
    lifts: list[tuple[str, str, str]] = []
    for ticket in convoy.tickets:
        park = ticket.get("park") or {}
        answer = park.get("answer")
        if ticket.get("status") == "closed" or park.get("origin") != ticket["id"] or not answer:
            continue
        exceptions = ticket.get("planning_exceptions") or []
        accepted = bool(exceptions) and isinstance(exceptions, list) and exceptions[-1].get("accepted")
        if park.get("cause") == "operator_request" or (park.get("cause") == "planning_exception" and accepted):
            lifts.append((ticket["id"], ticket["id"], answer["option"]))
    try:
        grouped = convoy.grouped or {}
        if grouped.get("lifts"):
            letter = request_answer(read_bead(grouped["bead"]), grouped["at"])
            if letter == grouped["lift_option"]:
                for ticket_id in grouped["lifts"]:
                    park = convoy.ticket(ticket_id).get("park") or {}
                    if park.get("origin") == ticket_id and park.get("cause") == PARK_EXHAUSTED:
                        lifts.append((ticket_id, grouped["bead"], letter))
    except Refusal as exc:
        out["refused"].append({"id": convoy.id, "reason": str(exc)})
    for ticket_id, request, letter in lifts:
        try:
            answer = state_write("lift-park", convoy.id, ticket_id, "--request", request, "--option", letter)
            out["lifted"].append({"id": ticket_id, "option": letter, "request": request, "lifted": answer["lifted"]})
        except Refusal as exc:
            out["refused"].append({"id": ticket_id, "reason": str(exc)})
    if lifts:
        convoy.load()


def parked_origins(convoy: Convoy) -> dict[str, list[str]] | None:
    """Each ticket that parks, with those parked behind it, when nothing
    but parked tickets is left in the convoy; None otherwise."""
    left = [t for t in convoy.tickets if t.get("status") != "closed"]
    if not left or not all(isinstance(t.get("park"), dict) and "origin" in t["park"] for t in left):
        return None
    origins: dict[str, list[str]] = {}
    for ticket in left:
        origins.setdefault(ticket["park"]["origin"], [])
        if ticket["park"]["origin"] != ticket["id"]:
            origins[ticket["park"]["origin"]].append(ticket["id"])
    return origins


def grouped_request(convoy: Convoy, origins: dict[str, list[str]]) -> tuple[dict[str, Any], str, list[str]]:
    """What the operator reads, once, for the whole convoy: each parked
    ticket and its cause. Returns the request, the full text and the
    tickets its first option lifts."""
    cause_of = {t["id"]: t["park"]["cause"] for t in convoy.tickets if isinstance(t.get("park"), dict)}
    detail_of = {t["id"]: t["park"].get("detail", "") for t in convoy.tickets if isinstance(t.get("park"), dict)}
    named, lines = [], []
    for origin, behind in origins.items():
        cause = PARK_CAUSES.get(cause_of.get(origin, ""), str(cause_of.get(origin)))
        named.append(f"{origin} ({cause})" + (f" + {', '.join(behind)}" if behind else ""))
        lines.append(f"- {origin} : {cause} — {detail_of.get(origin, '')}")
        lines += [f"- {ticket_id} : parqué derrière {origin} ({cause})" for ticket_id in behind]
    exhausted = [origin for origin in origins if cause_of.get(origin) == PARK_EXHAUSTED]
    lift = ({"option": "Relancer les tickets aux reprises épuisées",
             "consequence": "Chacun repart avec ses reprises ; les tickets qui l'attendent redeviennent démarrables."}
            if exhausted else
            {"option": "Répondre à la demande de chaque ticket parqué, sur sa propre ligne",
             "consequence": "Un ticket repart dès que sa propre demande a la réponse qui lève son parcage."})
    request = {
        "quoi": one_line(f"Convoi {convoy.id} : il ne reste que des tickets parqués — {' ; '.join(named)}"),
        "pourquoi": one_line(f"Plus aucun ticket du convoi {convoy.id} ne démarre ni ne fusionne sans ta réponse"),
        "que_faire": [lift, {"option": "Laisser ces tickets parqués",
                             "consequence": "Rien ne démarre ; le convoi reste ouvert, cette demande ne revient pas."}],
        "langue": operator_language(),
        "bloquant": True,
    }
    text = "\n".join([
        f"Il ne reste dans le convoi {convoy.id} que des tickets parqués : le script d'avancement "
        "(bin/convoy-advance) ne peut plus rien y démarrer.", "", "Tickets parqués et cause :", *lines, "",
        "Un ticket aux reprises épuisées repart quand tu réponds à cette demande par l'option qui le relance. "
        "Un ticket parqué par sa propre sortie (demande opérateur, Planning Exception) repart quand sa propre "
        "demande a sa réponse. Aucun ticket ne se reprend à la main."])
    return request, text, exhausted


def parkings_signature(convoy: Convoy) -> str:
    rows = sorted([t["id"], str(t["park"].get("cause")), str(t["park"].get("origin")), str(t["park"].get("at"))]
                  for t in convoy.tickets if t.get("status") != "closed" and isinstance(t.get("park"), dict))
    return "sha256:" + hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(rows, ensure_ascii=False).encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()


def record_grouped(convoy: Convoy, bead_id: str, signature: str | None = None, lifts: list[str] | None = None) -> None:
    argv = ["record-grouped-request", convoy.id, "--bead", bead_id]
    if signature:
        argv += ["--signature", signature]
    if lifts:
        # The door letters the options in order: the first one lifts.
        argv += ["--lift-option", "a", *(part for ticket_id in lifts for part in ("--lifts", ticket_id))]
    state_write(*argv)


def settle_grouped_request(convoy: Convoy) -> dict[str, Any] | None:
    """Spec §8, user story 54: one request per convoy, on a bead of its own,
    when nothing but parked tickets is left -- never one per ticket; raised
    once per set of parkings, withdrawn once a ticket may advance again."""
    try:
        origins = parked_origins(convoy)
        if origins is None:
            if not convoy.grouped:
                return None
            bead_id = convoy.grouped["bead"]
            passed(run([str(ESCALATION_BIN), "clear", bead_id]), "escalation-door clear")
            if read_bead(bead_id).get("status") != "closed":
                passed(run([GC_BIN, "--city", str(ROOT), "bd", "close", bead_id, "--reason",
                            f"Le convoi {convoy.id} n'est plus fait que de tickets parqués."]), "gc bd close")
            state_write("clear-grouped-request", convoy.id)
            return {"bead": bead_id, "withdrawn": True}
        signature = parkings_signature(convoy)
        if convoy.grouped and convoy.grouped.get("signature") == signature:
            return {"bead": convoy.grouped["bead"], "raised": False}
        request, text, lifts = grouped_request(convoy, origins)
        if convoy.grouped:
            bead_id = convoy.grouped["bead"]
            passed(run([GC_BIN, "--city", str(ROOT), "bd", "update", bead_id, "--append-notes", text]), "gc bd update")
        else:
            created = gc_json("bd", "create", f"Demande groupée : convoi {convoy.id}, il ne reste que des tickets parqués",
                              "-p", "1", "-t", "task", "-d", text, "--json")
            if isinstance(created, list):
                created = created[0] if created else None
            bead_id = created.get("id") if isinstance(created, dict) else None
            if not isinstance(bead_id, str) or not bead_id:
                raise Refusal("gc bd create n'a pas rendu l'identifiant du bead de la demande groupée")
            # Recorded before the escalation: a pass that fails after this
            # point is retried on the same bead, never on a second one.
            record_grouped(convoy, bead_id)
        passed(run([str(ESCALATION_BIN), "benjamin", bead_id, json.dumps(request, ensure_ascii=False)]),
               "escalation-door benjamin")
        record_grouped(convoy, bead_id, signature, lifts)
        return {"bead": bead_id, "raised": True}
    except Refusal as exc:
        return {"error": f"refus : {exc}"}


# --- the pass ----------------------------------------------------------------


@contextmanager
def advance_lock() -> Iterator[None]:
    """One pass at a time, Factory-wide: N is shared between the convoys."""
    lock_dir = Path(os.environ.get("CONVOY_ADVANCE_LOCK_DIR") or os.environ.get("XDG_RUNTIME_DIR") or "/tmp")
    lock_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    with (lock_dir / "agent-factory-convoy-advance.lock").open("w") as handle:
        fcntl.flock(handle.fileno(), fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        try:
            yield
        finally:
            fcntl.flock(handle.fileno(), fcntl.LOCK_UN)


def dispatch(convoy: Convoy, ticket_id: str, rig: str, settings: dict[str, Any]) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess[str]:
    argv = [str(DOOR_BIN), ticket_id, "--rig", rig, "--formula", settings["formula"], "--convoy", convoy.id]
    if settings["role"]:
        argv += ["--role", settings["role"]]
    return run(argv)


def advance_convoy(convoy: Convoy, settings: dict[str, Any], free: int, alive: set[str]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    out: dict[str, Any] = {"id": convoy.id, "started": [], "waiting": [], "deferred": [], "refused": [],
                           "resumed": [], "parked": [], "lifted": []}
    incident = settle_incident(convoy)
    if incident:
        out["incident"] = incident
    if convoy.unruled:
        out["signal"] = UNRULED
        out["unruled"] = convoy.unruled
        return out
    # The answers first: a ticket whose parking is lifted is resumed, and
    # those behind it started, by the same pass.
    settle_lifts(convoy, out)
    settle_resumes(convoy, settings, free, alive, out)
    for ticket in convoy.not_started():
        ticket_id = ticket["id"]
        park = ticket.get("park")
        if park:
            # Parked by a Ticket Exit (bin/ticket-exit), itself or behind the
            # ticket it waits for: not started until the parking is lifted.
            out["waiting"].append({"id": ticket_id, "reason": f"parqué ({park.get('cause')}, par {park.get('origin')})"})
            continue
        if len(out["started"]) + len(out["resumed"]) >= free:
            out["waiting"].append({"id": ticket_id, "reason": f"plafond N={settings['ceiling']} atteint"})
            continue
        blockers = open_blockers(ticket_id)
        if blockers:
            out["waiting"].append({"id": ticket_id, "reason": "bloqué par " + ", ".join(blockers)})
            continue
        rig = convoy.rigs.get(ticket_id)
        if not rig:
            out["refused"].append({"id": ticket_id, "reason": "le ticket ne nomme pas un seul projet connu de "
                                                              "config/projects sous « Target rigs »"})
            continue
        proc = dispatch(convoy, ticket_id, rig, settings)
        if proc.returncode == 0:
            out["started"].append(ticket_id)
        else:
            reason = (proc.stderr.strip() or proc.stdout.strip() or f"exit {proc.returncode}").splitlines()[-1]
            out["deferred" if proc.returncode == DOOR_DEFERRED else "refused"].append({"id": ticket_id, "reason": reason})
    # Once the starts are made: is anything but parked tickets left?
    if out["started"] or out["resumed"] or out["parked"] or out["lifted"]:
        convoy.load()
    grouped = settle_grouped_request(convoy)
    if grouped:
        out["grouped_request"] = grouped
    return out


def rig_profile(rig: str) -> Path:
    """The profile of the project that spans this rig: it declares the tests
    run on a merged result."""
    for path in sorted(DESCRIPTORS.glob("*.json")):
        try:
            rigs = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")).get("rigs")
        except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError, AttributeError):
            continue
        if isinstance(rigs, list) and rig in rigs:
            return path
    raise Refusal(f"aucun profil de projet de config/project-descriptors ne couvre le rig {rig} : "
                  "les tests à exécuter sur un résultat fusionné ne sont déclarés nulle part")


def merge_finished(convoy: Convoy) -> dict[str, Any] | None:
    """Spec §4: code merges the finished tickets of the convoy into the
    integration branch of its Spec, one at a time, through
    bin/spec-integration. None when the convoy has nothing to merge."""
    if not convoy.integration or not convoy.finished_unmerged():
        return None
    try:
        if not convoy.rig:
            raise Refusal(f"les tickets du convoi {convoy.id} ne nomment pas un seul projet connu de config/projects : "
                          "le dépôt de sa branche d'intégration est inconnu")
        proc = run([str(INTEGRATION_BIN), "merge", convoy.id, "--repo", str(convoy.repo),
                    "--profile", str(rig_profile(convoy.rig)), "--limit", str(MERGES_PER_PASS)])
        answer = parsed(proc, f"spec-integration merge {convoy.id}")
    except Refusal as exc:
        return {"error": f"refus : {exc}"}
    if not isinstance(answer, dict):
        return {"error": f"refus : spec-integration merge {convoy.id} a rendu une réponse illisible"}
    kept = ("branch", "integration", "takeover", "merged", "returned", "refused", "waiting", "error", "message", "unruled")
    return {name: answer[name] for name in kept if name in answer}


def settle_test_reviews(convoy: Convoy) -> dict[str, Any] | None:
    """Spec §5, §8: code, not a session, launches once more a review of
    criterion tests left without result, stops the ticket after that, and
    raises the stop to the operator, through bin/test-review. None when the
    convoy has no review to settle."""
    if not convoy.test_reviews_due():
        return None
    try:
        answer = parsed(run([str(TEST_REVIEW_BIN), "settle", convoy.id]), f"test-review settle {convoy.id}")
    except Refusal as exc:
        return {"error": f"refus : {exc}"}
    if not isinstance(answer, dict):
        return {"error": f"refus : test-review settle {convoy.id} a rendu une réponse illisible"}
    kept = ("launched", "relaunched", "pending", "stopped", "escalated", "deferred", "refused", "error")
    return {name: answer[name] for name in kept if answer.get(name)}


def settle_code_reviews(convoy: Convoy) -> dict[str, Any] | None:
    """Spec §6, §8: code, not a session, has each finished ticket reviewed
    before its merge, through bin/code-review. None when the convoy has no
    finished ticket to review."""
    if not convoy.code_reviews_due():
        return None
    try:
        answer = parsed(run([str(CODE_REVIEW_BIN), "settle", convoy.id, "--repo", str(convoy.repo)]),
                        f"code-review settle {convoy.id}")
    except Refusal as exc:
        return {"error": f"refus : {exc}"}
    if not isinstance(answer, dict):
        return {"error": f"refus : code-review settle {convoy.id} a rendu une réponse illisible"}
    kept = ("launched", "relaunched", "pending", "waiting", "stopped", "escalated", "deferred", "refused", "error")
    return {name: answer[name] for name in kept if answer.get(name)}


def settle_evaluations(convoy: Convoy) -> dict[str, Any] | None:
    """Spec §7, §8: code, not a session, has each finished ticket evaluated
    on the launched product before its merge, through bin/ticket-evaluation.
    None when the convoy has nothing to evaluate and no product to stop."""
    if not convoy.evaluations_due():
        return None
    try:
        answer = parsed(run([str(EVALUATION_BIN), "settle", convoy.id, "--repo", str(convoy.repo)]),
                        f"ticket-evaluation settle {convoy.id}")
    except Refusal as exc:
        return {"error": f"refus : {exc}"}
    if not isinstance(answer, dict):
        return {"error": f"refus : ticket-evaluation settle {convoy.id} a rendu une réponse illisible"}
    kept = ("launched", "relaunched", "pending", "waiting", "started", "refused_startup", "planning_exception",
            "stopped", "escalated", "deferred", "refused", "error")
    return {name: answer[name] for name in kept if answer.get(name)}


def settle_corrections(convoy: Convoy) -> dict[str, Any] | None:
    """Spec §8: code, not a session, opens the single correction round of a
    ticket its code review or its evaluation refused, sends it to one fresh
    author session, and stops the ticket still refused after it, through
    bin/correction-round. None when the convoy has no finished ticket, or
    when nothing was refused: the settlement then had nothing to say."""
    if not convoy.corrections_due():
        return None
    try:
        answer = parsed(run([str(CORRECTION_BIN), "settle", convoy.id, "--repo", str(convoy.repo)]),
                        f"correction-round settle {convoy.id}")
    except Refusal as exc:
        return {"error": f"refus : {exc}"}
    if not isinstance(answer, dict):
        return {"error": f"refus : correction-round settle {convoy.id} a rendu une réponse illisible"}
    kept = ("launched", "pending", "waiting", "stopped", "escalated", "deferred", "refused", "error")
    return {name: answer[name] for name in kept if answer.get(name)} or None


def check_fidelity(convoy: Convoy) -> dict[str, Any] | None:
    """Spec §9, condition 4: code, before the merge, runs the mechanical
    fidelity check of each finished interface ticket at the tip of its
    branch, through bin/ticket-end fidelity, which records the result on the
    ticket. None when the convoy has no such ticket to measure."""
    if not convoy.fidelity_due():
        return None
    try:
        if not convoy.rig:
            raise Refusal(f"les tickets du convoi {convoy.id} ne nomment pas un seul projet connu de config/projects : "
                          "le profil qui déclare ses écrans est inconnu")
        answer = parsed(run([str(TICKET_END_BIN), "fidelity", convoy.id, "--repo", str(convoy.repo),
                             "--profile", str(rig_profile(convoy.rig)), "--limit", str(FIDELITY_CHECKS_PER_PASS)]),
                        f"ticket-end fidelity {convoy.id}")
    except Refusal as exc:
        return {"error": f"refus : {exc}"}
    if not isinstance(answer, dict):
        return {"error": f"refus : ticket-end fidelity {convoy.id} a rendu une réponse illisible"}
    kept = ("checked", "waiting", "refused", "error", "message", "unruled")
    return {name: answer[name] for name in kept if answer.get(name)} or None


def settle_ticket_end(convoy: Convoy, merge: dict[str, Any] | None) -> dict[str, Any] | None:
    """Spec §9: code, and no agent, closes a ticket, through the ticket-end
    gate (bin/ticket-end settle): each merged ticket whose nine conditions
    are met is closed with the record of the gate; the others stay open,
    what they miss named. None when the convoy has no merged ticket left
    open and this pass merged none."""
    if not convoy.merged_open() and not (merge or {}).get("merged"):
        return None
    try:
        answer = parsed(run([str(TICKET_END_BIN), "settle", convoy.id, "--repo", str(convoy.repo)]),
                        f"ticket-end settle {convoy.id}")
    except Refusal as exc:
        return {"error": f"refus : {exc}"}
    if not isinstance(answer, dict):
        return {"error": f"refus : ticket-end settle {convoy.id} a rendu une réponse illisible"}
    kept = ("version", "closed", "open", "error", "message", "unruled")
    return {name: answer[name] for name in kept if answer.get(name)}


def one_pass(targets: list[str] | None, stopped_ok: bool = False) -> int:
    """`targets` None: every marked convoy that is open or was closed outside its commands."""
    with advance_lock():
        convoys = {convoy_id: Convoy(convoy_id) for convoy_id in targets or []}
        settings = load_settings()
        for convoy_id in marked_convoys():
            if convoy_id not in convoys:
                convoys[convoy_id] = Convoy(convoy_id)
        live = live_sessions()
        sessions = role_sessions(live)
        awaiting = sorted(ticket for convoy in convoys.values() for ticket in convoy.awaiting_a_session())
        occupied = sum(sessions.values()) + len(awaiting)
        free = max(0, settings["ceiling"] - occupied)

        results = []
        for convoy_id in targets if targets is not None else sorted(convoys):
            result = advance_convoy(convoys[convoy_id], settings, free, session_names(live))
            free -= len(result["started"]) + len(result["resumed"])
            results.append(result)

    # Outside the lock of the starts: the tests on a merged result take the
    # time they take, and bin/spec-integration holds its own lock per convoy.
    for result in results:
        if "unruled" in result:
            continue
        # The reviews first: a ticket whose verdict is already there is
        # merged by the same pass.
        reviews = settle_test_reviews(convoys[result["id"]])
        if reviews is not None:
            result["test_review"] = reviews
        code_reviews = settle_code_reviews(convoys[result["id"]])
        if code_reviews is not None:
            result["code_review"] = code_reviews
        evaluations = settle_evaluations(convoys[result["id"]])
        if evaluations is not None:
            result["evaluation"] = evaluations
        # Once both have answered: what they refused goes to one author
        # session, and a ticket still refused after its round is stopped.
        corrections = settle_corrections(convoys[result["id"]])
        if corrections is not None:
            result["correction"] = corrections
        # Before the merge: the fidelity of an interface ticket is measured
        # on the commit that merges (condition 4 of the ticket-end gate).
        fidelity = check_fidelity(convoys[result["id"]])
        if fidelity is not None:
            result["fidelity"] = fidelity
        merge = merge_finished(convoys[result["id"]])
        if merge is not None:
            result["integration"] = merge
        # After the merge: the gate closes what its nine conditions allow.
        closing = settle_ticket_end(convoys[result["id"]], merge)
        if closing is not None:
            result["ticket_end"] = closing

    unruled = any("unruled" in result for result in results)
    # A ticket returned or refused by the merge is an outcome of the pass; a
    # merge pass that could not run is a failure of it.
    refused = any(
        result["refused"] or "error" in result.get("incident", {}) or "error" in result.get("grouped_request", {})
        or any(key in result.get("integration", {}) for key in ("error", "message"))
        or any(key in result.get("test_review", {}) for key in ("error", "refused"))
        or any(key in result.get("code_review", {}) for key in ("error", "refused"))
        or any(key in result.get("evaluation", {}) for key in ("error", "refused"))
        or any(key in result.get("correction", {}) for key in ("error", "refused"))
        or any(key in result.get("fidelity", {}) for key in ("error", "refused", "message"))
        or any(key in result.get("ticket_end", {}) for key in ("error", "message"))
        for result in results
    )
    answer: dict[str, Any] = {
        "ok": not (unruled or refused), "ceiling": settings["ceiling"], "sessions": sessions,
        "awaiting_a_session": awaiting, "occupied": occupied, "convoys": results,
    }
    if unruled:
        answer["message"] = f"{UNRULED} : rien n'est démarré dans le convoi concerné"
    print(json.dumps(answer, indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False))
    return EXIT_UNRULED if unruled and not stopped_ok else EXIT_REFUSED if refused else 0


def main(argv: list[str]) -> int:
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog=PROGRAM, description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    parser.add_argument("convoy", nargs="?")
    parser.add_argument("--all", action="store_true", help="one pass on every open marked convoy, and on those closed outside acceptance or abandon")
    parser.add_argument("--check-only", action="store_true", help="exit 0 if a marked convoy is open or was closed outside acceptance or abandon, else 1")
    parser.add_argument("--stopped-ok", action="store_true",
                        help="exit 0, not 3, for a stopped convoy whose incident is raised (what the order runs)")
    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
    if sum((bool(args.convoy), args.all, args.check_only)) != 1:
        parser.error("exactly one of CONVOY, --all or --check-only is required")
    try:
        if args.check_only:
            return 0 if marked_convoys() else 1
        return one_pass(None if args.all else [args.convoy], args.stopped_ok)
    except NotNewFlow as exc:
        print(json.dumps(json.loads(str(exc)), indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False))
        return EXIT_NOT_NEW_FLOW
    except Refusal as exc:
        print(json.dumps({"ok": False, "error": f"refus : {exc}"}, indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False))
        return EXIT_REFUSED


if __name__ == "__main__":
    raise SystemExit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
